# Component folder structure

When creating or refactoring components (especially under `src/features/`), use this structure.

## One folder per component

- Each component lives in its **own folder** with a **kebab-case** name (e.g. `order-summary-row`, `payment-summary-section`).
- The folder is the component’s namespace; avoid flat files like `OrderSummaryRow.tsx` next to other components in the same group.

## Folder contents

Inside the component folder:

- **`index.tsx`** – The main component. Export the component (and optionally subcomponents that belong here).
- **`[component-name].types.ts`** – All props and related types for this component (e.g. `OrderSummaryRowProps` in `order-summary-row.types.ts`). Do not define props inline in the component file.
- No separate “index for re-export only” unless you need to expose multiple public entries; the default is one component per folder with `index.tsx` as the entry.

## Separators and small subcomponents

- **Separators** (e.g. list item separators) live in their **own file or folder**, not inline in the parent component.
  - Either a sibling folder (e.g. `summary-item-separator/index.tsx`) or a dedicated file (e.g. `payment-summary-separator.tsx` then moved into `payment-summary-separator/index.tsx` when converting to folders).
- Same idea for small, single-purpose UI pieces used only by one parent: give them a folder (or at least a file) and import from there.

## Naming

- **Folder names**: kebab-case (`order-summary-row`, `what-we-do-section`).
- **Types file**: `[folder-name].types.ts` (e.g. `order-summary-row.types.ts`).
- **Component names in code**: keep PascalCase (e.g. `OrderSummaryRow`, `PaymentSummarySection`).

## Barrel (index) at group level

- The parent group (e.g. `summary/`, `detail-sheet/`, `timeline/`) has an **`index.ts`** that re-exports only what consumers need (usually the main screen-level components), e.g. `export { OrderSummaryRow } from './order-summary-row';`.
- Internal subcomponents (e.g. separators, step cards) do not need to be in the barrel unless they are part of the public API.

## Import paths after refactor

- From a component **inside** a folder: use relative paths with one more `../` when going to feature root (e.g. `../../../types`, `../../../utils`).
- Between sibling folders: `../sibling-folder` (e.g. `../summary-item-separator`, `../payment-summary-separator`).

Apply this when you add new components or when the user asks to “refactor like the others” or “make it a folder / handle components like that.”
